    "markdown": "---\ntitle: datasets\n---\n\n\n\n```python\ndatasets(ref=None)\n```\n\nThe catalog: one row per dataset and scale.\n\n## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}\n\n| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n|--------|------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|        | pandas.DataFrame | Columns ``dataset`` (the id to pass to ``geo.load``), ``scale``, ``title``, ``years`` (e.g. ``\"2001–2020\"`` for an annual panel or ``\"2012, 2024\"`` for two periods), ``units`` (units with data), ``variables`` (how many), ``first_year``, ``last_year``, ``license``, ``categories`` and the ``csv`` and ``parquet`` paths. |\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q geo4bolivia\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\nimport plotly.express as px\n\ncat = geo.datasets()\ndisplay(cat[[\"dataset\", \"scale\", \"title\", \"years\", \"units\", \"variables\"]])\npx.bar(cat, x=\"dataset\", y=\"units\", color=\"years\", hover_name=\"title\",\n       title=\"Units with data per dataset\")\n```\n\n\n::: {#3a9b952d .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=